<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Kendi estimated the area of a fish pond on a farm in Kirinyaga from a plan drawn on squares. Each square stands for <m>{2}\,\text{m}</m> by <m>{2}\,\text{m}</m>. She counted <m>{23}</m> full squares and <m>{16}</m> part squares. Her working:</p><p>Step 1: number of squares <m>\approx {39}</m>.<br/>Step 2: area of one square <m>= {4}\,\text{m}^2</m>.<br/>Step 3: area <m>\approx {39} \times {4} = {156}\,\text{m}^2</m>.</p><p>Her working has one mistake.</p><p>(a) Which statement describes her mistake?</p><div><ol marker="(1)">
<li>Her working is correct.</li>
<li>She counted each part square as a whole square.</li>
<li>She left out the part squares.</li>
<li>She used the length of a side of a square instead of its area.</li>
<li>She used the perimeter of a square instead of its area.</li>
</ol>  </div><p>(b) Find the correct estimate of the area of the pond.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans2"/> <m>\text{m}^2</m>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Step</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Kendi</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Correct</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">1. Number of squares</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{39}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{23} + \tfrac{1}{2} \times {16} = {31}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">2. Area of one square</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4}\,\text{m}^2</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2} \times {2} = {4}\,\text{m}^2</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">3. Area</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{156}\,\text{m}^2</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{31} \times {4} = {124}\,\text{m}^2</m></cell></row></tabular><p>Kendi counted each part square as a whole square. A part square is, on average, about half covered, so it counts as <m>\tfrac{1}{2}</m>.</p><p>The area of the pond is about <m>{124}\,\text{m}^2</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>(2)</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>124</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>